
A Stream is a sequence of elements used to process data from collections in a declarative manner.
It allows operations such as filtering, mapping, sorting, and collecting without modifying the original collection.

Streams were introduced in Java 8 to simplify collection processing.
Before Streams, developers had to write multiple loops and temporary collections, making the code lengthy and harder to maintain.
Streams provide cleaner, more readable code and also support parallel processing.

Streams do not modify the original collection. They process the data and produce a new result.